openmediavault-qnapx39 (7.2.1) stable; urgency=low

  * LCD: one page per network port with its IPv4 address and link (read
    from the kernel, so it no longer depends on the ip command), and one
    page per disk bay with disk, temperature, state, size and model.
  * LCD: Shutdown/Reboot menu on the last page, with a confirmation;
    it can be turned off.

 -- Rui <zrcz180@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:30:00 -0000

openmediavault-qnapx39 (7.2.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Front LCD on the TS-639 Pro (A125 on /dev/ttyS1, powered by GPIO
    GP10): host name and IP address, status, temperatures, fans, disks
    and uptime. SELECT shows the next page, ENTER the previous one. The
    backlight goes off after a set time without a press and comes back
    on with a new problem.

 -- Rui <zrcz180@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:10:00 -0000

